    "name": "Geamparaua de la Murfatlar",
    "abc": "X:72\nT:Geamparaua de la Murfatlar\nM:7/8\nN:Dobrogea region (Bulgarian influence). So says Daniel200235, by email.\nN:I have this from Alistair Cochrane in the middle of Sweden, who says :-\nN: I got it from an old vinyl LP by a band called Vargavinter, Stockholm\nN: experimental folkies from the seventies. Marie Selander, Tuomo Haapala,\nN: Kjell Westling... can't remember who else. The name is maybe suspect.\nN: Geampara, though, is a kind of dance that turns up now and then with\nN: the 4+3 rhythm\nO:Rumania\nZ:Richard Robinson <URL:http://www.qualmograph.org.uk/contact.html>\nS:Alistair Cochrane\nK:A min ^c_B\n cAcA cde |  d2 dc BAG |  \\\n cAcA cde |  d2 dc BAG |1 \\\n cAcA cde |  d2 dc def |  \\\n gffe dcd |  e2 eA eAA :|2\n gffe ded |  c2 cA BAG |  \\\n ABBA GFG |  A2 A2 Ace |: \\\n a2 a2 Aca |  g2 g2 Acg  |  \\\n f2 fe ded |  c2 cA BAG  |\n f2 fe ded |  c2 cA BAG  |1 \\\n f2 fe dcd |  e2 e2 Ace :|2\\\n ABBA GFG  |  A2AE AEE |:\n e2 dc def |  gfga gfe |  \\\n gffe ded | c2 cA BAG  |\n effe ded |  c2 cA BAG |1 \\\n effe dcd |  e2 eA eAA :|2\\\n ABBA GFG |  A2 AE AEE |]"
