    "abc": "X:16\nT:Haymakers. JBa.15\nM:6/8\nL:1/8\nQ:3/8=100\nS:Joseph Barnes MS,Carlisle,1762.\nR:Jig\nO:England\nA:North-West - Carlisle\nN:As usual, no time or key signature,Not many bar lines either and not\nN:much resemblence to the Playford Haymakers.  Fortunately it does bear a\nN:strong resemblance in the MS of  John Miller of Perth, 1799..and the\nN: version in Vicker's MS... photocopy\nN:very unclear Do I hear faint echoes of 'Off she goes' - 'Pop goes the\nN:Weasel'..  Edited with reference to version in John Miller, Perth MS\nN:1799..CGr.\nZ:vmp.C.Graebe.\nB:Village Music project, Barnes, Joseph\n%%Mirrorred-From:http://www.village-music-project.org.uk/abc/barnes_j.abc\nK:C major\nGB AcA cB G2 AFD G2B2 AcA BdB G2 ||!\nG2g2 gf d2 efg dBG G2g2 gf d2 efg d2 ||!\nc2e2 dBG AcA cBG ce dBG AcA G2 ||!\nzzzzzzzzzzz|!\nK:G major\n\nG2B AcA |  cBG AFD|  G2B AcA |  BdB G3 ||!\nG2g gfd | efg dBG  |G2g gfd | efg d3 ||!\nc2e dBG |  AcA cBG |  c2e dBG |  AcA G3 |]"
