    "name": "Portugese. JC.006",
    "abc": "X:6\nT:Portugese. JC.006\nR:Misc\nS:John Clare,Poet,Helpston. (1793-1864)\nN:MS time sig is 5/4 in ms. This is convincing proof to me that\nN:Clare,Poet\nN:wasn't merely copying tunes from printed sources all the time , and\nN:that he may have been trying to make an accurate transcription of a\nN:performance. Whether he was entirely successful or not, given some of\nN:the grammatical problems with some of the tunes, is problematical, to\nN:say the least. Nevertheless, this tune and others in this MS would\nN:repay some very close study with fiddle in hand. CGP...\nO:England\nA:Northamptonshire\nZ:vmp.P. Headford\nM:2/4\nL:1/8\nQ:1/4=120\nB:Village Music project, Clare, John\n%%Mirrorred-From:http://www.village-music-project.org.uk/abc/clare_J.abc\nK:D major\nd2fff|\\\ngfe f|e/d/ cde|cde d f>ff|g>fe f|df gfd2|cB cd:|!\n|:e2e|cA defe|e2e2|cA defe|ageg e|ef e|de fgd|edc A2c2d2:|"
